# Open States v3 API key — free, register at https://open.pluralpolicy.com/
#
# Powers the bill list in the "Statewide Campaign Goals" banner and the district
# lookup behind "Email your state legislators". The bill list is *discovered*
# with this key, not just annotated: there is no list of bills in the repo, so
# without a key the banner has no bills to show at all.
#
# Optional, and it degrades honestly. No key: the banner says live tracking
# isn't configured on this deployment, and the action center links out to
# leg.mn.gov instead of prefilling a mailto. It never shows an empty bill list
# as though the legislature were quiet.
#
# RATE LIMIT — 10 requests per minute. Measured, not documented anywhere
# obvious: the 11th call in a minute returns
#   429 {"detail":"exceeded limit of 10/min"}
# and the window clears after about a minute idle. One cold refresh of the
# tracker spends 4 (one for the session list, three for pages of results), so
# the thing that breaks it is refreshes overlapping, not daily volume.
# ~/lib/edgeCache.ts handles that with single-flight, a six-hour freshness
# window, a two-week last-good fallback, and a one-minute backoff after any
# failure. If you change the query in ~/data/legislation.ts, re-check the page
# count — every extra page is another request against that ceiling.
#
# Also worth knowing: a `q=` search combined with `sort=` and NO `session=`
# filter makes Open States search-then-sort the whole state corpus. That takes
# 17-27s and their gateway answers 502 before it finishes. Keep the session
# filter.
#
# Local dev: copy this to .env (or .dev.vars for the Cloudflare platform
# proxy). Production: set it as a Worker secret, NOT in this file —
#   wrangler secret put OPENSTATES_API_KEY
OPENSTATES_API_KEY=""
